			"id": "agent-analysis-hvigor-build-engine-config",
			"interpretation": "Maintenance contract (configuration-asset): hvigor/ is a single-file leaf boundary holding hvigor/hvigor-config.json5, the project-level config of the Hvigor build engine. Responsibility: pin engine modelVersion 5.0.0 and tune engine behavior via declared 'properties' that disable the in-memory cache (hvigor.enableMemoryCache=false, hvigor.pool.cache.capacity=0) and cap pool/ArkCompile concurrency (hvigor.pool.maxSize=5, ohos.arkCompile.maxSize=3); execution, logging, debugging, and nodeOptions blocks are fully commented, so documented defaults apply. Relations: no source imports this file; it is consumed by the Hvigor engine selected by root hvigorfile.ts via '@ohos/hvigor-ohos-plugin' (appTasks), its modelVersion should stay aligned with oh-package.json5 (5.0.0), and the engine acts on products declared in root build-profile.json5. Maintenance rules: keep the file valid JSON5, do not rename existing property keys, bump modelVersion only together with oh-package.json5, and treat uncommenting knobs as deliberate engine behavior changes. No build execution or tool behavior is claimed.",
			"kind": "analysis",
			"limitations": ["Whether the Hvigor engine at modelVersion 5.0.0 actually honors the four 'properties' keys (hvigor.pool.cache.capacity, hvigor.pool.maxSize, ohos.arkCompile.maxSize, hvigor.enableMemoryCache) is unproved: the repo contains no engine source or documentation for them.","The inline comments stating defaults for execution, logging, debugging, and nodeOptions options are unverified vendor annotations; the effective defaults at the pinned engine version were not observed.","No evidence that a build consuming this configuration succeeds, nor that the memory-tuning values are appropriate for any particular build machine; only textual alignment of modelVersion with oh-package.json5 was checked.","The relationship of this project-level config to any user- or CI-level hvigor settings that could override it was not examined."],
